meta {
  name: Convert currency
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/convert?have=AUD&want=USD&amount=899
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  have: AUD
  want: USD
  amount: 899
}

docs {
  # Convert currency

  Converts an amount between the currencies Lpaecomms transacts in, using live
  exchange rates from API Ninjas. Backs the currency converter mashup and is
  available to the mobile and desktop clients.

  This endpoint exists as a server-side proxy so the provider API key stays in
  `NINJA_API_KEY` and never reaches a client. Rates are cached in process for
  one hour per currency pair, so repeated calls for the same pair do not consume
  the provider's free-plan quota.

  ## Auth

  None for the caller. The service authenticates to the provider itself with the
  `X-Api-Key` header, read from the `NINJA_API_KEY` environment variable.

  ## Parameters

  Query parameters, all required:

  - `have` (string, required) — source currency. One of `AUD`, `USD`, `GBP`, `EUR`.
  - `want` (string, required) — target currency. Same set as `have`.
  - `amount` (number, required) — amount in the source currency. Must be greater than zero.

  Converting a currency into itself is valid and returns a rate of 1 without
  calling the provider.

  ## Responses

  ### 200 OK — conversion performed

  {
    "have": "AUD",
    "want": "USD",
    "amount": 899,
    "rate": 0.659,
    "converted": 592.44,
    "cached": false
  }

  Fields:

  - `rate` (number) — exchange rate applied.
  - `converted` (number) — amount in the target currency, rounded to cents.
  - `cached` (boolean) — true when the rate came from the one-hour cache rather
    than a fresh provider call.

  ### 400 Bad Request — invalid parameters

  A currency outside the supported set, or an amount that is not a positive
  number.

  {
    "statusCode": 400,
    "error": "Bad Request",
    "message": "Parameters \"have\" and \"want\" must be one of: AUD, USD, GBP, EUR.",
    "validation": [],
    "url": "/api/v1/convert?have=AUD&want=JPY&amount=899",
    "method": "GET"
  }

  ### 502 Bad Gateway — provider unavailable

  The provider is unreachable, timed out after 5 seconds, or answered a non-2xx
  status. Provider authentication failures (401/403) are logged server-side and
  surface here too: a client is never told the key is wrong.

  {
    "statusCode": 502,
    "error": "Bad Gateway",
    "message": "The currency provider is unavailable.",
    "validation": [],
    "url": "/api/v1/convert?have=AUD&want=USD&amount=899",
    "method": "GET"
  }

  ### 503 Service Unavailable — not configured

  `NINJA_API_KEY` is not set in this environment. The rest of the service keeps
  working; only conversion is unavailable.

  {
    "statusCode": 503,
    "error": "Service Unavailable",
    "message": "Currency conversion is not configured.",
    "validation": [],
    "url": "/api/v1/convert?have=AUD&want=USD&amount=899",
    "method": "GET"
  }
}
